---
import ContentPage from "@/layouts/ContentPage.astro";
import DocSection from "@/components/DocSection.astro";
import { APP_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from "@/lib/appConfig";

export const prerender = true;

// Bump when the terms' substance changes; "Changes to these terms" promises it.
const EFFECTIVE = "November 10, 2026";
---

{
  /* Unlisted like /privacy-policy: linked from the footer, kept out of search
    results. public/robots.txt disallows the fetch. */
}
<ContentPage
  title={`Terms of Service — ${APP_NAME}`}
  description={`The terms for using the ${APP_NAME} app and website.`}
  heading="Terms of Service"
  noindex
>
  <p class="text-muted mt-4 text-sm">Effective {EFFECTIVE}</p>

  <div class="text-muted mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
    <p>
      Welcome to {APP_NAME}. These terms cover your use of the {APP_NAME} app and the website at{
        " "
      }
      <a href="https://waterrun.app" class="underline underline-offset-4">waterrun.app</a>, both run
      by me, James Mitofsky. By using {APP_NAME}, you agree to them. If you don't agree, please
      don't use it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <DocSection heading={`Using ${APP_NAME}`}>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} is free to use. You may use the app and the website for your own, non-commercial purposes,
      subject to these terms. How {APP_NAME} handles your information is explained in the{" "}
      <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection heading="Your safety comes first">
    <ul>
      <li>
        Fountain information is gathered by the community and may be out of date or wrong. A
        fountain shown as working may be broken, gone, or switched off for the season. Don't count
        on finding water: carry what you need.
      </li>
      <li>
        {APP_NAME} doesn't test water quality. Use your own judgement before drinking from any fountain.
      </li>
      <li>
        Routes are planned automatically and may cross busy roads, closed paths or private land.
        Follow traffic laws and local rules, stay aware of your surroundings, and don't look at your
        phone while crossing a street.
      </li>
      <li>
        Running is physical exercise. Run within your limits, and talk to a doctor if you're unsure
        whether it's safe for you.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection heading="Your contributions">
    <p>
      The fountain updates you send are published to OpenStreetMap, the free public map {APP_NAME}'s
      fountain data lives on, under your own OpenStreetMap account. They're governed by
      OpenStreetMap's{" "}
      <a href="https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Licence/Contributor_Terms">contributor terms</a> and made
      available under the{" "}
      <a href="https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/">Open Database License</a>. I don't claim
      ownership of them.
    </p>
    <p>
      You're responsible for what you send. Report only what you've seen for yourself, and don't
      include personal information about yourself or anyone else in notes.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection heading="Your OpenStreetMap account">
    <p>
      Signing in uses your OpenStreetMap account, which is provided by the OpenStreetMap Foundation
      under its own{" "}
      <a href="https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Terms_of_Use">terms of use</a>. Keep your account
      secure; you're responsible for what's sent under it.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection heading="Acceptable use">
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>send false, misleading or deliberately damaging updates to the map;</li>
      <li>
        send automated or bulk requests to {APP_NAME}'s servers, or use them for anything other than{
          " "
        }
        {APP_NAME} itself;
      </li>
      <li>
        interfere with, overload, or try to get around the limits of {APP_NAME} or its servers;
      </li>
      <li>harass anyone or cause distress to anyone in connection with {APP_NAME};</li>
      <li>use {APP_NAME} for anything unlawful.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      I may block access for anyone who breaks these rules, to protect {APP_NAME} and the people who use
      it.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection heading="Ownership">
    <p>
      The {APP_NAME} name, logo, design and text belong to James Mitofsky. All rights are reserved, except
      where stated otherwise. Map data is ©{" "}
      <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap contributors</a>, available
      under the Open Database License.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection heading={`Services ${APP_NAME} relies on`}>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} depends on services run by others, including OpenStreetMap, volunteer-run map data and
      route planning servers, and map image providers. I don't control them and can't promise they'll
      always be available or accurate. Their own terms apply to your use of them.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection heading="Changes and availability">
    <p>
      I may change, suspend or stop any part of {APP_NAME} at any time, with or without notice. You can
      stop using it at any time: sign out and delete the app.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection heading="No warranties">
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} is provided "as is", without any representations or warranties, express or implied. I
      make no representations or warranties about {APP_NAME} or the information and materials it provides,
      including that fountain information is accurate, complete or current, or that routes are safe or
      passable.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection heading="Limitation of liability">
    <p>
      To the fullest extent the law allows, James Mitofsky won't be liable to you for any indirect,
      special or consequential loss, or for any loss of revenue, income, profits or anticipated
      savings, arising from your use of {APP_NAME} or in connection with it, including relying on its
      fountain information or routes.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection heading="Links">
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} links to other websites. I'm not responsible for their contents, and a link doesn't mean
      I endorse the site. Use them at your own risk.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection heading="Changes to these terms">
    <p>
      I may revise these terms at any time by posting a new version on this page, with a new
      effective date. By continuing to use {APP_NAME} after a change, you agree to the revised terms.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection heading="Governing law">
    <p>
      These terms are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the United States,
      and you irrevocably submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts located there.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection heading="Contact">
    <p>
      If you have any questions about these terms, email me at{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </DocSection>
</ContentPage>
